        },
        "OTHER LABORATORY TESTS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OTHER LABORATORY TESTS",
          "canonical_heading": "OTHER LABORATORY TESTS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CSF analysis—nonspecific findings.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cytology—ultrasound (US)-guided fine-needle biopsy can provide diagnostic sample. Cytologic features of malignant",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "IMAGING": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "IMAGING",
          "canonical_heading": "IMAGING",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "resected nerve sheath tumors in dogs.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Survey radiographs—well-positioned survey",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dexamethasone 0.1–0.25 mg/kg q24h or radiographs may allow visualization of an prednisone 0.5–1 mg/kg q12–24h can be enlarged intervertebral foramen; most often used to provide short-term improvement.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "unrewarding.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "US—can identify a mass in",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Gabapentin 5–20 mg/kg q8–12h can be cases where axillary palpation is unrewarding in used for analgesia in cases of neuropathic distally located tumors. Patient sedation allows",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "pain.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Pregabalin 2–4 mg/kg q12h can be better positioning and US-guided fine-needle used in cases refractory to gabapentin. aspiration biopsy. Tumor echogenicity is variable.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Myelography—if the neoplasm has invaded the vertebral canal, an intradural extra medullary pattern can be seen. Due to the location of neoplasms, myelography is diagnostic in approximately 50% of dogs.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Nerve sheath tumors are locally invasive",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CT and MRI—to visualize proximal or",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "and rarely metastasize.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Postoperative local distal limb tumors. Hyperintensity on recurrence is common (up to 72% of cases). T2-weighted images is the most common MRI pattern. MPNSTs usually show contrast enhancement on both CT and MRI. Due to the high soft tissue characterization, MRI is the diagnostic modality of choice.",
              "pdf_page": 1058,
              "printed_page": 976,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
